{"name":"Jazz Brass","hex":"#d48740","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jazz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical art form rooted in West African cultural and musical expression and in the African American blues tradition, with diverse influences over time, commonly characterized by blue notes, syncopation, swing, call and response, polyrhythms and improvisation.","Energy, excitement, excitability."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To destroy; to ruin.","To play (jazz music)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jazz"},{"term":"brass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic alloy of copper and zinc used in many industrial and plumbing applications.","A memorial or sepulchral tablet usually made of brass or latten: a monumental brass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of brass, of or pertaining to brass.","Of the color of brass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jazz","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz is a music genre that originated in the African-American communities of New Orleans, Louisiana, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Its roots are in blues, ragtime, European harmony, African rhythmic rituals, spirituals, hymns, marches, vaudeville song, and dance music. Since the 1920s Jazz Age, it has been recognized as a major form of musical expression in both traditional and popular music. Jazz is characterized by swing and blue notes, complex chords, call and response vocals, polyrhythms and improvisation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz","wikidata":"Q8341"},{"title":"Brass","blocks":[{"text":"Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc, in proportions which can be varied to achieve different colours and mechanical, electrical, acoustic, and chemical properties, but copper typically has the larger proportion, generally 2⁄3 copper and 1⁄3 zinc. In use since prehistoric times, it is a substitutional alloy: atoms of the two constituents may replace each other within the same crystal structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg/330px-Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brass","wikidata":"Q39782"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brass lectern with an eagle, attributed to Aert van Tricht, Limburg (Netherlands), circa 1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_(Netherlands)%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg/500px-Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg/1280px-Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe